      gridTitle:'GF(p) coordinate plane', gridHint:'Horizontal position x is the share number and vertical position y is the share value. Shares are issued for x=1 through n; x=0 marks candidate secrets, and columns beyond n show more evaluations. This coordinate plane starts at zero: the bottom-left cell is (0,0). Moving right increases x by one; moving up increases y by one.',
      gridInteractionHint:'Hover to see (x,y). Drag a point, or select it and tap a cell in its column. Up and down arrow keys move one cell.',
      gridLabel:'Finite-field coordinate plane of shares and candidates', cell:'cell', sharePoint:'Share point', fewSharesExample:'With fewer than k−1 shares, the curve is not unique. Faint points show one example from the current polynomial.', realTitle:'Move a real-number curve', realWarning:'The real-number curve illustrates points and the intercept. Ordinary integer arithmetic leaks remainders. Use the finite-field coordinate plane above for the actual calculation.',
